    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW21mXvibxgZ5NzrmRV92h1on)_\n\n**Before:** checkbox lists under a `Tasks` heading in the vault are invisible to the agenda and org-gtd, and TODO-like words (`DOING`, `WAITING`, `STARTED`, ...) that are not declared in `init.el` or in the file are plain text to Org.\n\n**After:** new module `sp-org-normalise` (`libraries/modules/custom/`, literate doc `docs/tangles/custom/sp-org-normalise.org`, listed in `docs/main.org`, loaded from `init.el` after `sp-org-issues`).\n- `M-x sp-org-normalise-inventory`: every keyword-like heading word with heading and file counts, how many files do not recognise it, and what the mapping table does with it.\n- `M-x sp-org-normalise-preview`: report buffer of proposed changes per file; `RET` visits a change. Writes nothing.\n- `M-x sp-org-normalise-run`: the preview, then per file yes / no / choose each change / quit. Buffers are left modified and unsaved (`sp-org-normalise-save-after-apply` to change).\n- Checkbox items under a `Tasks` heading become child headings: `[ ]` TODO, `[X]` DONE, `[-]` PROG. Nested lines stay in the body. A checklist under a heading that already has a keyword is left alone.\n- `sp-org-normalise-keyword-map` (editable) rewrites `DOING`, `WAITING`, `CANCELLED`, ... to the org-gtd set; words not in it are only reported. A `#+todo:` line is proposed for files that would otherwise use an unknown keyword; files with their own sequence are only noted.\n- Code blocks and drawers are never read. All `defcustom`s are in the group `sp-org-normalise`. No external packages.\n\n**Checked** (headless Emacs 29.3, container only, fake vault in a temp directory): 24 ERT tests in `tests/sp-org-normalise-test.el` (tangled from the doc), plus a manual run of inventory, preview and apply on a small fake vault. The tests started red and were fixed (case-folding of the keyword regexp; undeclared words wrongly triggering a `#+todo:` line).\n\n**Not checked:** the interactive prompts (`read-char-choice`, `y-or-n-p`) and the report buffer in a real Emacs, and anything on the real vault, TRAMP or Windows paths. The default map rewrites `DOING` and `WAITING`, which `sp-org-taskman-extra` currently sets globally; remove them from the map if you want to keep those.\n\nRun it with `emacs -Q --batch -L libraries/modules/custom -l tests/sp-org-normalise-test.el -f ert-run-tests-batch-and-exit` from the `init.el` folder.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01Rh8KvNdDsHexMokeq2BxN2)_",
